      {
        "id": "human-a11y-review",
        "statement": "A human completed an end-to-end accessibility review of this component.",
        "verification": "manual",
        "note": "2026-10-31: reviewed live in Storybook (Default, Example, ForcedColors). The root is aria-hidden with no role, every SVG has focusable=\"false\", there are no focusable descendants and no text reaches the accessibility tree. Under prefers-reduced-motion the cross-fade stops and each cell keeps its first glyph, so the composition stays static rather than blank; animate={false} gives the same still frame. Cells swap at most every 0.6 s over a small area, well below the WCAG 2.3.1 flash threshold. Marks inherit the text colour and switch to CanvasText in forced colors. Because the loop runs indefinitely with no on-page pause, use it as a small accent beside content, not as a large hero behind reading text (WCAG 2.2.2).",
        "reviewedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    ]
